  "notes": [
    "Raw shared-checksum uses the same chunk size, block size and shared scratch allocation as ANS, including coalesced 16-byte cp.async transfers. Each chunk emits its own checksum; no grid-wide atomic bottleneck.",
    "Compression sizes count actual stream bytes. Aligned allocation, metadata and scratch are reported separately. Padding never counts as compressed payload.",
    "Vendor float16 mode receives the original BF16 byte pattern without any numerical conversion and passed exact byte reconstruction across the full bank.",
    "Rearranged-format checksum timing does not include reverse transformation, making it an optimistic bound for later matrix multiplication.",
